  "rationale": "This inscription is an administrative and financial account from the sanctuary of Apollo on Delos, likely dating to the late 4th or early 3rd century BC based on the calendar and names. It records the management of sacred funds by the hieropoioi, including the collection of interest on loans, payments for religious sacrifices, and expenditures for the construction and decoration of statues. The text is organized chronologically by the Delian calendar. The presence of a string at the end resembling the name of Antoninus Pius is highly unusual for a Delian account of this period and may represent a later addition or a misreading of the stone.",
